<title>UK: Genfinance sets 2.0 bln Luf Bel 20-linked bond.</title>
<headline>Genfinance sets 2.0 bln Luf Bel 20-linked bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Banque Generale du Luxembourg and Generale Bank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENFINANCE LUXEMBOURG</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  GENERALE BANK</p>
<p> AMT    2.0 BLN LUF   COUPON     *ZERO     MATURITY    28.MAR.03</p>
<p> TYPE   INDEX-LINKED  ISS PRICE  100.0     PAY DATE    15.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K)  50-250</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 FORCE MAJ  YES	 GOV LAW     LUX</p>
<p> MGT/UND    =	   SELL CONC  =	   PRAECIPUUM  0.25</p>
<p> NOTES	*THERE IS AN ANNUAL KLIK OPTION ON BRUSSELS EXCHANGE</p>
<p>		 INDEX BEL 20 WITH A 100.0 PCTPARTICIPATION RATIO</p>
<p>		 (CAPPED AT 18.0 PCT ANNUALLY)</p>
<p>		 REDEMPTION PRICE IS 100.0 PCT PLUS THE VALUE OF THE</p>
<p>		 KLIK OPTION AT MATURITY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
